/Title (CORS \(Cross-Origin Resource Sharing\) is a browser security mechanism. By default, browsers enforce a "same-origin policy", meaning a web page cannot request data from a different domain. CORS allows servers to explicitly permit trusted domains \(clients\) to access their resources using specific HTTP headers.)
